```
#
# Analyze Slurm account hierarchy, users, PIs and project accounts.
# ============================
#          ACCOUNT TREE
# ============================
##root
##└── dept_technology_and_society
##    └── pi_feng
##        ├── pn_cs
##        │   ├── @feng
##        │   └── @zhang
##        └── pn_math
##            └── @li
#
```

```
$ ./slurm_account-users-v3.py  --help
usage: slurm_account-users-v3.py [-h] [--summary] [--department PATTERN] [--pi-filter PATTERN] [--pn PATTERN] [--user PATTERN] [--department-summary] [--pi] [--pi-compact] [--tree] [--accounts] [--users]
                                    [--validate]

Analyze Slurm account hierarchy, users, PIs and project accounts.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --summary             Show overall account/user summary.
  --department, --dept PATTERN
                        Filter departments using wildcard pattern.
  --pi-filter PATTERN   Filter pi_* accounts using wildcard pattern.
  --pn PATTERN          Filter pn_* accounts using wildcard pattern.
  --user PATTERN        Filter users using wildcard pattern.
  --department-summary, --dept-summary
                        Show department-centric summary.
  --pi                  Show detailed PI-centric summary.
  --pi-compact          Show compact PI summary.
  --tree                Show account hierarchy including users.
  --accounts            List accounts grouped by type.
  --users               List users by account.
  --validate            Validate account hierarchy.

Examples:

  Show everything:
    slurm_account-users-v3.py

  Overall summary:
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --summary

  All departments:
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --dept 'dept_*'

  Specific department:
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --dept 'dept_computer_science'

  Departments beginning with "dept_com":
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --dept 'dept_com*'

  PIs beginning with "pi_f":
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --pi-filter 'pi_f*'

  Specific project:
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --pn 'pn_cs'

  Projects beginning with "pn_cs":
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --pn 'pn_cs*'

  Users beginning with "feng":
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --user 'feng*'

  Users containing "zh":
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --user '*zh*'

  Compact PI report for matching PIs:
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --pi-compact --pi-filter 'pi_f*'

  Detailed PI report:
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --pi --pi-filter 'pi_f*'

  List matching accounts:
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --accounts --pi-filter 'pi_f*'

  List matching users:
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --users --user 'feng*'

  Combine filters:
    slurm_account-users-v3.py --pi-compact --dept 'dept_cs*'

Wildcard syntax follows Python fnmatch/shell-style matching:
    *   matches any number of characters
    ?   matches one character
    [abc] matches one character from the set
```
